{
 "id": "C-F255",
 "level": "complete",
 "title": "validate_workflow refuses an out-of-range tonal control, naming it and its range, and accepts the ends; a non-numeric string for a float grade control is refused, and a variable: reference to one is not",
 "note": "C-F252's one-grade-step shape. 'Names its range' is the range in any of the usual spellings ('-1.0 and 1.0', '-1 to 1', '[-1, 1]' and so on). `fade: \"0.5\"` 'may be accepted' asserts nothing, so it is not sent. `highlights: null` may be refused or read as unset; only 'not a crash' is asserted (no tool error, a verdict present). 'Queues no job' is the refusal with no job_id, and the workspace's job total unchanged across the call: a job another session queues in regression-complete in that second would fail it. The run_workflow sends acknowledged_cost=true as the prose does, and comes after step 1 has seen validate refuse the same arguments.",
 "steps": [
  {
   "label": "range: shadows 2 is refused, naming it and its range",
   "call": "validate_workflow",
   "args": {
    "workspace": "regression-complete",
    "workflow": {
     "id": "qa-c-f252",
     "steps": [
      {
       "name": "grade",
       "task": {
        "command": "grade",
        "arguments": {
         "media": "asset:qa-cast/priya-portrait.jpg",
         "shadows": 2
        }
       },
       "result": {
        "content_type": "image/png"
       }
      }
     ]
    }
   },
   "expect": [
    {
     "path": "valid",
     "eq": false
    },
    {
     "path": "errors",
     "any_contains": [
      "\"path\": \"steps[0].task.arguments.shadows\""
     ]
    },
    {
     "path": "errors[*].message",
     "contains": "shadows"
    },
    {
     "path": "errors[*].message",
     "contains_any": [
      "-1.0 and 1.0",
      "-1 and 1",
      "-1.0 to 1.0",
      "-1 to 1",
      "[-1.0, 1.0]",
      "[-1, 1]"
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
